    15	- RULE: The production evidence gate now requires at least 2000 samples (20× the original 100-cycle minimum), the existing fixed 10-sample allocator warmup, post-warmup and trailing 1000-sample maximum drawup no greater than `256 KiB` (1% of the upper 25 MiB provisional envelope), and either a trailing plateau or an observed post-warmup release. Maximum drawup measures each upward excursion from the running minimum, so a large release is not itself a failure. Raw evidence records every parameter, transition count, jump cycle, ownership counter, and sample. Positive plateau and bounded-oscillation tests plus unreleased late-rise and oversized-high-water negative tests bind the classifier; the original rise-plus-plateau negative remains.
